  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday) \nIssued at 140 PM CDT Mon May 25 2026\n\nThe low pressure mentioned in the short term portions of this \ndiscussion will move to the east by late Wednesday. Another much \nstronger low develops across the western U.S. by Thursday. This will \nlargely leave us in between the two systems resulting in more \nsettled weather for Thursday and Friday. A couple of isolated rain \nshowers cannot be totally ruled out, but the overall chances are \nvery low (20%). \n\nThe deep low pressure over the western U.S. may slowly drift to the \neast and northeast by this weekend. This may be just enough support \nto generate more scattered thunderstorms on Saturday and Sunday. \nThis remains rather uncertain at this point given significant \ndifferences in the long range model solutions.",
